# Target C-II — two-leaf outer energy excludes `t<=1.843645`

**Date:** 2026-09-15  
**Status:** proof-only full-core Type-II strengthening  
**Scope:** full-core/no-macroscopic-container Type-II branch  
**Dependencies:** scope-safe matched atomic gap `g=0.007707`; hostile-audited residual stability/shared retention/complement incidence; `t<=1.844` phasewise retained-outer theorem; hostile-audited correlated center/leaf capacity; repaired cross-phase O--O endpoint-energy theorem  
**Certificate:** `research/verify_target_c_two_leaf_outer_energy_exclusion_t1843645.py`  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** `STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.`

The merged theorem excludes `t=(q-k)/D<=1.84364`.  Re-optimizing the same two-leaf architecture with the current scope-safe atomic constant

\[
C_{707}=2\sqrt{\Delta_2}+0.007707,
\qquad
\Delta_2={\pi\over2\sqrt3},
\]

shows that the argument still has rigorous room at

\[
\boxed{T=1.843645.}
\]

The safe rounded constants used below are

\[
H=0.00036,
\qquad
W_0=1.912693,
\qquad
E_0=0.9068995,
\]

\[
U_0=0.530,
\qquad
Z_0=2.21939,
\qquad
A_0=0.7035,
\]

and the final good O--O pair weight in each leaf is larger than `0.1365D-o(D)`.
The exact certificate leaves more than `5.4e-4 D` in the final outer-energy contradiction.

Therefore, at the stated proof-only scope,

\[
\boxed{
\liminf_{D\to\infty}{q-k\over D}\ge1.843645.
}
\tag{E645.1}
\]

No C-II or Level-I closure is claimed.

---

## 1. Residual stability is in scope and forces `h<0.00036`

Write

\[
t={q-k\over D},
\qquad
x={\kappa\over2},
\qquad
\delta={d_{out}\over D},
\]

and

\[
h=U_{net}-C_{707}.
\]

The residual-stability theorem is stated for `U_net<=2.013`.  The already-proved `t<=1.844` phase theorem gives retained mass above `0.616D` in each exact dominant phase.  Hence total retained dominant mass is above `1.848D`, and the three-well bathtub inequality gives

\[
\delta\ge F(1.848)-o(1),
\qquad
F(z)=z-6\sin(z/6).
\]

The exact certificate checks `F(1.848)>0.029` and therefore, at `t<=T`,

\[
U_{net}
\le {9t\over2}-2\pi-2\delta
<1.956<2.013.
\]

Thus the audited residual estimate applies:

\[
R:=U_{net}-M\le1.05h,
\tag{E645.2}
\]

where `M` is the dominant exact-orbit mass.

The exact envelope is

\[
2\delta+x+h
=R_t:={9t\over2}-2\pi-C_{707}.
\tag{E645.3}
\]

The survivor capacity is increasing in `t` and decreasing in `x,h`; the inherited derivative bounds remain

\[
Q_x<-2.7,
\qquad
Q_h<-2.5.
\tag{E645.4}
\]

At the adverse point `t=T`, `x=0`, `h=H=0.00036`, the exact verifier proves

\[
F\!\left(
\pi-{T\over2}-1.05H
-{1.05^2H^2\over2(1-(R_T-H)/2)}
\right)
-{R_T-H\over2}
>3.99\times10^{-6}.
\tag{E645.5}
\]

Hence every survivor with `t<=T` must satisfy

\[
\boxed{0\le h<0.00036-o(1).}
\tag{E645.6}
\]

Consequently

\[
M<C_{707}+0.00036<1.912693+o(1),
\tag{E645.7}
\]

and, since all residual exact orbits together carry at most `R^2/4` crossing mass,

\[
\boxed{E_{dom}>0.9068995-o(1).}
\tag{E645.8}
\]

The exact outward slacks in (E645.7)--(E645.8) are respectively above `3.86e-7` and `1.46e-7`.

