## 2. Both leaf phase masses are below `0.530D`

Write the dominant exact-orbit phase masses as

\[
C\ge U\ge V,
\qquad
C+U+V=M.
\]

Assume `U>=U_0=0.530`.  Replace the total mass and crossing target adversely by

\[
W_0=1.912693,
\qquad
E_0=0.9068995.
\]

Generic center capacity excludes `C<=U_0` and, with the slightly shifted high-center cutoff

\[
C\ge1.0442,
\]

also excludes the high-center tail.

For

\[
C\le W_0-2U_0=0.852693,
\]

the hostile-audited strong aggregate phase-star capacity applies.  At the endpoint its exact deficit from `E_0` is greater than `0.00697`.

On the remaining interval

\[
0.852693<C<1.0442,
\]

the strong physical `1/10` center/leaf pair theorem is valid for both leaves.  Its worst excess ratio remains below the branch threshold `sqrt(20/29)` by more than `0.0389`.

Fixing `W=W_0` and `U=U_0` is adverse for the correlated capacity.  Put

\[
V=W_0-C-U_0
\]

and

\[
\begin{aligned}
G(C)=&\ C(U_0+V)\\
&-{1\over10}\left(1-{V\over C}\right)(C+U_0-K)^2\\
&-{1\over10}\left(1-{U_0\over C}\right)(C+V-K)^2,
\qquad K={2\over\sqrt3}.
\end{aligned}
\tag{E645.9}
\]

The inherited derivative identity gives `G''<-2`.  Using the tangent point `C=0.931447`, exact outward arithmetic gives

\[
\max G(C)<E_0-1.21\times10^{-5}.
\tag{E645.10}
\]

This contradicts (E645.8).  Therefore

\[
\boxed{U,V<0.530-o(1).}
\tag{E645.11}
\]

---

## 3. Retained dominant outer mass exceeds `2.21939D`

Let `z` be the retained dominant outer-occurrence mass, `p` the retained complement O--O pair mass, and `e_c` the selected complement terminal energy.  The audited shared-retention system gives

\[
z+p\ge\pi-{t\over2}-x-1.05h-o(1),
\tag{E645.12}
\]

\[
p(1-\delta)-{e_c\over2}
\le{1.05^2h^2\over2}+o(1),
\tag{E645.13}
\]

and

\[
F(z)+e_c\le\delta+o(1).
\tag{E645.14}
\]

Assume `z<=Z_0=2.21939`.  Capped retention is increasing in `z`, so replace `z` by `Z_0`.  On the energy boundary `delta=F(Z_0)`, (E645.3) gives

\[
x+h=h_*:=R_T-2F(Z_0).
\]

The exact enclosure gives

\[
0<h_*<0.000352301< H.
\tag{E645.15}
\]

On this boundary the capped-retention excess increases with `h`, so the adverse point is `h=h_*`, `x=0`.  Exact outward arithmetic gives

\[
Z_0
+{1.05^2h_*^2\over2(1-F(Z_0))}
-\pi+{T\over2}+1.05h_*
<-1.01\times10^{-5}.
\tag{E645.16}
\]

The `delta<F(Z_0)` side is no better by the same negative `Q_x,Q_h` derivatives.  Thus

\[
\boxed{z>2.21939-o(1).}
\tag{E645.17}
\]

